IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 13, SECTIONS 103 TO 107 (inspection, enquiry, arrest, the offence of
-- obstruction).  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * This Part speaks mostly of what officials may or must do.  It is encoded for the individual it is done to or asked of:
--     what an official may do to a person or a workplace, what the person must do when asked, what the officer must give or show.
--   * Seam S14 is NOT taken: s 105(1)(a) turns on what the inspecting officer REASONABLY SUSPECTS, not on an offence in fact, so
--     it takes the suspicion as a plain input (NOTES.md, Seams).
--   * Section 105D (equipping inspecting officers) is administration with no effect on any person; it has no function here.
--   * A plain BOOLEAN or NUMBER answer is a date or count comparison and carries no legal "no".

§ `Part 13 -- the powers of the Commissioner and inspecting officers (s 103)`

GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(1) helper: the official is the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` MEANS
    official EQUALS `Official: the Commissioner for Labour` OR official EQUALS `Official: an inspecting officer`

-- s 103(1): "The Commissioner or any inspecting officer has, for the purposes of this Act, power to do all or any of the following".
-- src:4145 | 103.—(1) The Commissioner or any inspecting officer has, for the
-- src:4146 | purposes of this Act, power to do all or any of the following:
@ref s 103(1) (src:4145-4146)
GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1) the official has the powers in this subsection` MEANS
    IF `s 103(1) helper: the official is the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` official
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the powers are those of "The Commissioner or any inspecting officer"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 103(1)(a): "to enter and search, by day or by night, any premises or part thereof when he or she has reasonable cause to
-- believe that evidence of the commission of an offence under this Act or of a civil contravention can be found therein".
-- src:4148 | (a) to enter and search, by day or by night, any premises or part
-- src:4149 | thereof when he or she has reasonable cause to believe that
-- src:4150 | evidence of the commission of an offence under this Act or
-- src:4151 | of a civil contravention can be found therein;
@ref s 103(1)(a) (src:4148-4151)
GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
      `the official has reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of an offence under the Act or of a civil contravention can be found in the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1)(a) the official may enter and search the premises` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 103(1) helper: the official is the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` official)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the powers are those of "The Commissioner or any inspecting officer"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the official has reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of an offence under the Act or of a civil contravention can be found in the premises`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when he or she has reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of an offence"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 103(1)(aa): "to enter without previous notice at any reasonable time any place of employment for the purpose of
-- conducting any audit in relation to the terms and conditions of employment of any employee".
-- src:4153 | (aa) to enter without previous notice at any reasonable time any
-- src:4154 | place of employment for the purpose of conducting any
-- src:4155 | audit in relation to the terms and conditions of employment
-- src:4156 | of any employee;
@ref s 103(1)(aa) (src:4153-4156)
GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
      `the place is a place of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is conducting an audit in relation to the terms and conditions of employment of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1)(aa) the official may enter the place of employment without previous notice` MEANS
    IF `s 103(1) helper: the official is the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` official
       AND `the place is a place of employment` AND `the time is a reasonable time`
       AND `the purpose is conducting an audit in relation to the terms and conditions of employment of an employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to enter a place of employment at a reasonable time for the purpose of an audit of the terms and conditions of employment
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 103(1)(b): "to examine orally any person reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to
-- the carrying out of the provisions of this Act, and to reduce into writing the answer given or statement made by that person".
