      `the person is reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1)(b) the official may examine the person orally and reduce the answer or statement into writing` MEANS
    IF `s 103(1) helper: the official is the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` official
       AND `the person is reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to examine a person "reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 103(1)(c): "to require any person whom the Commissioner or inspecting officer has reason to believe has any document,
-- including documents of identity or documents containing information relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of this Act,
