-- src:4188 | removed for this purpose;
@ref s 103(1)(f) (src:4184-4188)
GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
      `the materials or substances are used or handled by employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer or the employer's representative has been notified of the samples taken or removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1)(f) the official may retain the samples for analysis` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for samples of materials and substances used or handled by employees
        IF NOT (`s 103(1) helper: the official is the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` official AND `the materials or substances are used or handled by employees`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the employer or the employer's representative has been notified of the samples taken or removed` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that the employer or the employer's representative must be notified of any such samples"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 103(1)(g): "to take such photographs, or audio or video recording, as the Commissioner or inspecting officer thinks
-- necessary, of the premises and persons reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the
-- carrying out of the provisions of this Act".
