GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
      `the photograph or recording is of the premises or of persons reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official thinks the photograph or recording necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1)(g) the official may take the photograph or audio or video recording` MEANS
    IF `s 103(1) helper: the official is the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` official
       AND `the photograph or recording is of the premises or of persons reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act`
       AND `the official thinks the photograph or recording necessary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to take such photographs or recordings "as the Commissioner or inspecting officer thinks necessary" of the premises and of persons reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts
    ELSE NOTHING

