§ `Part 13 -- arrest, restraint, search and the disposal of what is taken (ss 105 to 106A)`

-- s 105(1): "Any inspecting officer may arrest without warrant any person whom the inspecting officer reasonably suspects (a) is
-- committing or has committed an offence under section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34; or (b) has abetted the commission of
-- any offence mentioned in paragraph (a)."  The power turns on the officer's reasonable suspicion, not on an offence in fact.
-- src:4227 | 105.—(1) Any inspecting officer may arrest without warrant any
-- src:4228 | person whom the inspecting officer reasonably suspects —
-- src:4230 | (a) is committing or has committed an offence under
-- src:4231 | section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34; or
-- src:4233 | (b) has abetted the commission of any offence mentioned in
-- src:4234 | paragraph (a).
@ref s 105(1) (src:4227-4234)
GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
      `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person is committing or has committed an offence under section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person has abetted the commission of such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(1) the inspecting officer may arrest the person without warrant` MEANS
    IF official EQUALS `Official: an inspecting officer`
       AND (`the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person is committing or has committed an offence under section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34`
            OR `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person has abetted the commission of such an offence`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "Any inspecting officer" over a person whom the officer reasonably suspects of an offence under section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34, or of abetting it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105(2): "Any inspecting officer may arrest without warrant any person who is an officer or a member of a body corporate or an
-- unincorporated association or a partner of a partnership and whom the inspecting officer reasonably suspects has consented to,
-- connived in or due to neglect on that person's part caused the commission of an offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a)."
-- src:4238 | (2) Any inspecting officer may arrest without warrant any person
-- src:4239 | who is an officer or a member of a body corporate or an
-- src:4240 | unincorporated association or a partner of a partnership and whom
-- src:4241 | the inspecting officer reasonably suspects has consented to, connived
-- src:4242 | in or due to neglect on that person’s part caused the commission of an
-- src:4243 | offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a).
@ref s 105(2) (src:4238-4243)
GIVEN official IS AN `Official or body the Act names`
      `the person is an officer or a member of a body corporate or an unincorporated association, or a partner of a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person consented to, connived in or by neglect caused the commission of an offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(2) the inspecting officer may arrest the person without warrant` MEANS
    IF official EQUALS `Official: an inspecting officer`
       AND `the person is an officer or a member of a body corporate or an unincorporated association, or a partner of a partnership`
       AND `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person consented to, connived in or by neglect caused the commission of an offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over an officer or member of a body corporate or unincorporated association, or a partner, whom the officer reasonably suspects of consenting to, conniving in or causing by neglect an offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105(3): "An inspecting officer making an arrest without warrant must, without unnecessary delay and subject to subsection (5),
-- produce the person arrested before a Magistrate's Court."
-- src:4247 | (3) An inspecting officer making an arrest without warrant must,
-- src:4248 | without unnecessary delay and subject to subsection (5), produce the
-- src:4249 | person arrested before a Magistrate’s Court.
@ref s 105(3) (src:4247-4249)
GIVEN `an inspecting officer arrested the person without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was released on bail or on his or her own bond under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(3) the inspecting officer must produce the person arrested before a Magistrate's Court` MEANS
    IF `an inspecting officer arrested the person without warrant` AND (NOT `the person was released on bail or on his or her own bond under subsection (5)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of an inspecting officer making an arrest without warrant, "subject to subsection (5)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105(4): "An inspecting officer must not detain in custody a person arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in
-- the circumstances, and the period must not exceed 48 hours exclusive of the time necessary for the journey from the place of
-- arrest to the Magistrate's Court."
-- src:4253 | (4) An inspecting officer must not detain in custody a person
-- src:4254 | arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in the
-- src:4255 | circumstances, and the period must not exceed 48 hours exclusive
-- src:4260 | of the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the
-- src:4261 | Magistrate’s Court.
@ref s 105(4) (src:4253-4261)
GIVEN `the hours the person arrested without warrant has been detained, not counting the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court` IS A NUMBER
      `the detention is longer than is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(4) the inspecting officer may detain the person in custody for that long` MEANS
    IF `the detention is longer than is reasonable in the circumstances`
       OR `the hours the person arrested without warrant has been detained, not counting the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court` GREATER THAN 48
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An inspecting officer must not detain in custody a person arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids detention for longer than is reasonable or for more than 48 hours; it never says that a shorter detention is lawful, so the twin `s 105(4) the inspecting officer must not detain the person in custody for that long` below asks the text's own question
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The twin that asks the text's own question, with its own verb ("must not detain"): the forbidden
-- detention is one longer than is reasonable, or one that exceeds 48 hours; a detention of exactly 48
-- hours or less that is reasonable is outside what the text forbids (rulings of 2026-11-05; fork F18).
-- src:4253 | (4) An inspecting officer must not detain in custody a person
-- src:4254 | arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in the
-- src:4255 | circumstances, and the period must not exceed 48 hours exclusive
-- src:4260 | of the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the
-- src:4261 | Magistrate’s Court.
@ref s 105(4) (src:4253-4261)
GIVEN `the hours the person arrested without warrant has been detained, not counting the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court` IS A NUMBER
      `the detention is longer than is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(4) the inspecting officer must not detain the person in custody for that long` MEANS
    IF `the detention is longer than is reasonable in the circumstances`
       OR `the hours the person arrested without warrant has been detained, not counting the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court` GREATER THAN 48
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not detain in custody a person arrested without warrant for longer than is reasonable in the circumstances"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

