GIVEN `the restraint is more than is necessary to prevent the person's escape` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105B(1) the person arrested may be subjected to the restraint` MEANS
    IF `the restraint is more than is necessary to prevent the person's escape`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person arrested must not be subjected to more restraint than is necessary"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids restraint beyond what is necessary to prevent escape; it does not say that restraint within it is lawful
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105B(2): "An inspecting officer may use handcuffs or any similar means of restraint on a person arrested to prevent him or
-- her from (a) inflicting any bodily injury to himself, herself or others; (b) damaging any property; (c) creating any
-- disturbance; or (d) escaping from custody."
-- src:4291 | (2) An inspecting officer may use handcuffs or any similar means
-- src:4292 | of restraint on a person arrested to prevent him or her from —
-- src:4294 | (a) inflicting any bodily injury to himself, herself or others;
-- src:4296 | (b) damaging any property;
-- src:4298 | (c) creating any disturbance; or
-- src:4300 | (d) escaping from custody.
@ref s 105B(2) (src:4291-4300)
GIVEN `the restraint is to prevent the person inflicting bodily injury to himself, herself or others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restraint is to prevent the person damaging property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restraint is to prevent the person creating a disturbance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restraint is to prevent the person escaping from custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105B(2) the inspecting officer may use handcuffs or a similar means of restraint` MEANS
    IF `the restraint is to prevent the person inflicting bodily injury to himself, herself or others`
       OR `the restraint is to prevent the person damaging property`
       OR `the restraint is to prevent the person creating a disturbance`
       OR `the restraint is to prevent the person escaping from custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection lists four purposes and does not say that handcuffs may not be used for another
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105B(3): "The handcuffs or similar means of restraint must not be used for the purpose of punishment."
-- src:4304 | (3) The handcuffs or similar means of restraint must not be used for
-- src:4305 | the purpose of punishment.
@ref s 105B(3) (src:4304-4305)
GIVEN `the restraint is used for the purpose of punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105B(3) the handcuffs or similar means of restraint may be used` MEANS
    IF `the restraint is used for the purpose of punishment`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be used for the purpose of punishment"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids use for punishment; it does not say that any other use is lawful
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105C(1): "When a person is arrested, the inspecting officer making the arrest may search the person and take possession of
-- all articles (other than necessary wearing apparel) found upon the person that the inspecting officer has reason to believe
-- were connected with the offence for which the person is being arrested."
-- src:4311 | 105C.—(1) When a person is arrested, the inspecting officer
-- src:4312 | making the arrest may search the person and take possession of all
-- src:4313 | articles (other than necessary wearing apparel) found upon the person
-- src:4318 | that the inspecting officer has reason to believe were connected with
-- src:4319 | the offence for which the person is being arrested.
@ref s 105C(1) (src:4311-4319)
GIVEN `the person is arrested by the inspecting officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the article is necessary wearing apparel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspecting officer has reason to believe the article was connected with the offence for which the person is being arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105C(1) the inspecting officer may take possession of the article found upon the person` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is arrested by the inspecting officer`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a person is arrested, the inspecting officer making the arrest may search the person and take possession of all articles"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        IF (NOT `the article is necessary wearing apparel`)
           AND `the inspecting officer has reason to believe the article was connected with the offence for which the person is being arrested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over articles "other than necessary wearing apparel" found upon the person that the officer has reason to believe were connected with the offence
        ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105C(2): "Whenever it is necessary to cause a person to be searched, the search must be made by an inspecting officer of the
-- same sex as the person, with strict regard to decency."
-- src:4323 | (2) Whenever it is necessary to cause a person to be searched, the
-- src:4324 | search must be made by an inspecting officer of the same sex as the
-- src:4325 | person, with strict regard to decency.
@ref s 105C(2) (src:4323-4325)
GIVEN `the inspecting officer is of the same sex as the person to be searched` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105C(2) the inspecting officer may make the search` MEANS
    IF NOT `the inspecting officer is of the same sex as the person to be searched`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the search must be made by an inspecting officer of the same sex as the person"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection requires an officer of the same sex; it does not itself give the power to search, which is subsection (1)'s
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The twin that asks the text's own question ("the search must be made by an inspecting officer of the
-- same sex"), with its "Whenever it is necessary to cause a person to be searched" counted as "where"
-- (rulings of 2026-11-05; "whenever" is on the ruled list; fork F18): where no search is necessary the
-- requirement does not arise.
-- src:4323 | (2) Whenever it is necessary to cause a person to be searched, the
-- src:4324 | search must be made by an inspecting officer of the same sex as the
-- src:4325 | person, with strict regard to decency.
@ref s 105C(2) (src:4323-4325)
GIVEN `it is necessary to cause the person to be searched` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105C(2) the search must be made by an inspecting officer of the same sex as the person` MEANS
    IF `it is necessary to cause the person to be searched`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Whenever it is necessary to cause a person to be searched"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 105E: "An inspecting officer making any arrest may take from the person arrested any offensive weapons which that person has
-- about his or her person."
-- src:4339 | 105E. An inspecting officer making any arrest may take from the
-- src:4340 | person arrested any offensive weapons which that person has about
-- src:4341 | his or her person.
@ref s 105E (src:4339-4341)
GIVEN `the inspecting officer is making an arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the article is an offensive weapon the person arrested has about his or her person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105E the inspecting officer may take the offensive weapon from the person arrested` MEANS
    IF `the inspecting officer is making an arrest` AND `the article is an offensive weapon the person arrested has about his or her person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of an inspecting officer making an arrest, over offensive weapons the person has about his or her person
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 105F: "If a person in lawful custody escapes or is rescued, the inspecting officer from whose custody that person escaped or
-- was rescued may immediately pursue and arrest that person in any place within Singapore and deal with him or her as the
-- officer might have done on the original arrest."
-- src:4347 | 105F. If a person in lawful custody escapes or is rescued, the
-- src:4348 | inspecting officer from whose custody that person escaped or was
-- src:4349 | rescued may immediately pursue and arrest that person in any place
-- src:4350 | within Singapore and deal with him or her as the officer might have
-- src:4351 | done on the original arrest.
@ref s 105F (src:4347-4351)
GIVEN `the person in lawful custody escaped or was rescued from the custody of the inspecting officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105F the inspecting officer may immediately pursue and arrest the person in any place within Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the person in lawful custody escaped or was rescued from the custody of the inspecting officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person in lawful custody escapes or is rescued"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 106: "A person must not, except in the performance of his or her duties, reveal any manufacturing or commercial secrets which
-- may at any time come to his or her knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer."
-- src:4357 | 106. A person must not, except in the performance of his or her
-- src:4358 | duties, reveal any manufacturing or commercial secrets which may at
-- src:4359 | any time come to his or her knowledge in the course of his or her duty
-- src:4360 | as an inspecting officer.
-- src:4362 | Disposal of documents, articles, etc.
@ref s 106 (src:4357-4362)
GIVEN `the secret is a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person reveals it in the performance of his or her duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 the person may reveal the manufacturing or commercial secret` MEANS
    IF `the secret is a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer` AND (NOT `the person reveals it in the performance of his or her duties`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must not, except in the performance of his or her duties, reveal any manufacturing or commercial secrets"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of revealing manufacturing or commercial secrets that came to the person's knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer, except in the performance of his or her duties
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 106A(1): documents, articles and things the Commissioner or an inspecting officer takes possession of under this Part (a) where
-- produced in any criminal trial, must be dealt with in accordance with section 364 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010; and
-- (b) in any other case, must be returned to the owner or reported to a Magistrate.
DECLARE `s 106A(1) What must be done with the thing taken` IS ONE OF
    `s 106A(1)(a) deal with it in accordance with section 364 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 106A(1)(b) return it to the owner or report it to a Magistrate`

-- src:4364 | 106A.—(1) Any document, article or thing that the Commissioner
-- src:4365 | or an inspecting officer takes possession of under this Part must —
-- src:4370 | (a) where the document, article or thing is produced in any
-- src:4371 | criminal trial, be dealt with in accordance with section 364
-- src:4372 | of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010; and
-- src:4374 | (b) in any other case, be returned to the owner or reported to a
-- src:4375 | Magistrate.
@ref s 106A(1) (src:4364-4375)
GIVEN `the Commissioner or an inspecting officer took possession of the document, article or thing under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document, article or thing is produced in a criminal trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`s 106A(1) What must be done with the thing taken`)
`s 106A(1) what must be done with the document, article or thing` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner or an inspecting officer took possession of the document, article or thing under this Part`
    THEN
        IF `the document, article or thing is produced in a criminal trial`
        THEN JUST `s 106A(1)(a) deal with it in accordance with section 364 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
        ELSE JUST `s 106A(1)(b) return it to the owner or report it to a Magistrate`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for a document, article or thing that the Commissioner or an inspecting officer takes possession of under this Part
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 106A(2): "Where the report of any document, article or thing is made to a Magistrate under subsection (1)(b), the Magistrate
-- may order the document, article or thing (a) to be forfeited; or (b) to be disposed of in any manner that the Magistrate thinks fit."
