-- src:4386 | fit.
@ref s 106A(2) (src:4379-4386)
GIVEN `the report of the document, article or thing was made to a Magistrate under subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106A(2) the Magistrate may order the document, article or thing to be forfeited or to be disposed of` MEANS
    IF `the report of the document, article or thing was made to a Magistrate under subsection (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the report of any document, article or thing is made to a Magistrate under subsection (1)(b)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

