§ `Part 13 -- the offence of obstruction (s 107)`

-- s 107(a): "without reasonable excuse, neglects or refuses to produce any document or article as required under section 103".
-- src:4399 | (a) without reasonable excuse, neglects or refuses to produce
-- src:4400 | any document or article as required under section 103;
@ref s 107(a) (src:4399-4400)
GIVEN `the person neglected or refused to produce a document or article as required under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(a) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person neglected or refused to produce a document or article as required under section 103` AND (NOT `the person had a reasonable excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is neglecting or refusing, without reasonable excuse, to produce a document or article as required under section 103
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 107(b): "makes to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer exercising the powers under section 103 a statement, either
-- orally or in writing, which is false in a material particular".
