-- src:4404 | either orally or in writing, which is false in a material
-- src:4405 | particular; or
@ref s 107(b) (src:4402-4405)
GIVEN `the person made to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer exercising the powers under section 103 a statement, oral or in writing, that is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(b) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person made to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer exercising the powers under section 103 a statement, oral or in writing, that is false in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is a statement, oral or in writing, false in a material particular, made to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer exercising the powers under section 103
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 107(c): "otherwise hinders or obstructs the Commissioner or an inspecting officer in the exercise of the powers under section 103".
